<article class="env-lemma" id="07RQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07RQ">Lemma <span data-tag="07RQ">32.8.14</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Situation <a href="/tag/081D" data-tag="081D">32.8.1</a>. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is a monomorphism, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f_0$ is locally of finite type, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $f_ i$ is a monomorphism for some $i \geq 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that a morphism of schemes $V \to W$ is a monomorphism if and only if the diagonal $V \to V \times _ W V$ is an isomorphism (Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01L3" data-tag="01L3">26.23.2</a>). The morphism $X_0 \to X_0 \times _{Y_0} X_0$ is locally of finite presentation by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0818" data-tag="0818">29.22.12</a>. Since $X_0 \times _{Y_0} X_0$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated (Schemes, Remark <a href="/tag/0816" data-tag="0816">26.21.18</a>) we conclude from Lemma <a href="/tag/081E" data-tag="081E">32.8.11</a> that $\Delta _ i : X_ i \to X_ i \times _{Y_ i} X_ i$ is an isomorphism for some $i \geq 0$. For this $i$ the morphism $f_ i$ is a monomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>